.TH "GTESTER" 1 "" "GLib" "gtester"
.SH NAME
gtester \- test running utility
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.ad l
.hy 0
.HP 8
\fBgtester\fR [OPTION...] [testprogram]
.ad
.hy

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
\fBgtester\fR is a utility to run unit tests that have been written using the GLib test framework\&.

.PP
When called with the \fB\-o\fR option, \fBgtester\fR writes an XML report of the test results, which can be converted into HTML using the \fBgtester\-report\fR utility\&.

.SH "OPTIONS"

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help and exit

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
print version information and exit

.TP
\fB\-\-g\-fatal\-warnings\fR
make warnings fatal

.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-going\fR
continue running after tests failed

.TP
\fB\-l\fR
list paths of available test cases

.TP
\fB\-m=\fIMODE\fR\fR
run test cases in \fIMODE\fR, which can be one of: 

.RS

.TP
\fBperf\fR
run performance tests

.TP
\fBslow\fR, \fBthorough\fR
run slow tests, or repeat non\-deterministic tests more often

.TP
\fBquick\fR
do not run slow or performance tests, or do extra repeats of non\-deterministic tests (default)

.TP
\fBundefined\fR
run test cases that deliberately provoke checks or assertion failures, if implemented (default)

.TP
\fBno\-undefined\fR
do not run test cases that deliberately provoke checks or assertion failures

.RE
.IP
 

.TP
\fB\-p=\fITESTPATH\fR\fR
only run test cases matching \fITESTPATH\fR 

.TP
\fB\-s=\fITESTPATH\fR\fR
skip test cases matching \fITESTPATH\fR 

.TP
\fB\-\-seed=\fISEEDSTRING\fR\fR
run all test cases with random number seed \fISEEDSTRING\fR 

.TP
\fB\-o=\fILOGFILE\fR\fR
write the test log to \fILOGFILE\fR 

.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
suppress per test binary output

.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
report success per testcase

.SH "SEE ALSO"

.PP
 \fBgtester\-report\fR(1) 

